workqueue: keep one idle worker per pool instead of two

Local patch (debloat batch 24, 2026-10-17). Every per-CPU pool (2 per CPU)
keeps two idle kworkers forever; one is enough on this laptop. About 48
fewer kernel threads at idle on 24 CPUs (estimated -1.4 MiB). The only
cost is creating a worker a little more often under bursty load.

--- a/kernel/workqueue.c
+++ b/kernel/workqueue.c
@@ -979,7 +979,7 @@
 	int nr_idle = pool->nr_idle + managing; /* manager is considered idle */
 	int nr_busy = pool->nr_workers - nr_idle;
 
-	return nr_idle > 2 && (nr_idle - 2) * MAX_IDLE_WORKERS_RATIO >= nr_busy;
+	return nr_idle > 1 && (nr_idle - 1) * MAX_IDLE_WORKERS_RATIO >= nr_busy;
 }
 
